examples.solution_text:
$3\times3=9$, so the split of $6$ is incorrect. Split $6$ into $2\times3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\node (a) at (0,2) {$42$};
\node (b) at (-1.2,1) {$6$};
\node (c) at (1.2,1) {$7$};
\node (d) at (-2,0) {$2$};
\node (e) at (-0.4,0) {$3$};
\draw (a)--(b) (a)--(c) (b)--(d) (b)--(e);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Every leaf is now prime.
$42=2\times3\times7$.
End branches at primes; do not split $7$ into $1\times7$, because $1$ is not prime.
